# Hash routing

This app uses **Vue Router hash mode** (`vueRouterMode: 'hash'` in `quasar.config.js`) for GitHub Pages / static hosting.

## Full URLs (browser, docs, MCP navigation)

Use the hash segment:

- `http://localhost:9000/#/heroes` — not `http://localhost:9000/heroes`
- `http://localhost:9000/#/relationships`
- Deployed: `{base}/#/heroes`

Bare paths without `/#/` load the SPA shell but **not** the intended route.

## In-app code (unchanged)

Vue Router handles the hash internally — these stay as path-only:

- `router-link to="/heroes"`, `q-route-tab to="/heroes"`
- `route.path === '/heroes'` for active state
- Child routes in `routes.js`: `path: 'heroes'`

## Dev server

The user runs `quasar dev` externally; it hot-reloads. Do not suggest restarting to pick up code changes (see `no-dev-server.mdc`).
